 "notes": "Curve traced from the blue 95% CL exclusion line in Fig. 3(a) (rasterized panel embedded in Fig3.eps of the e-print), left y-axis: nucleon EDM coupling g_d (GeV^-2) vs mass (neV). Paper's HEDM = g_d a E*.I/I with oscillating EDM d = g_d a0, identical to the canonical g_d (d_n = g_d a), so no conversion. Extracted plateau ~9.6e-4 GeV^-2 agrees with the quoted headline bound |g_d| < 9.5e-4 GeV^-2 over 162-166 neV; steep walls at the scan-band edges (~161.7 and ~166.6 neV) are included. The paper also bounds the gradient coupling |g_aNN| < 2.8e-1 GeV^-1 (right axis of same figure); the EDM coupling is the primary CASPEr-electric result. DM density assumed: rho_DM = 3.6e-42 GeV^4 = 0.47 GeV/cm^3 (not rescaled). Axis calibration from tick pixels (x: 161/163/165/167 neV; y: 1e0..1e-3 decade ticks, 172.8 px/decade).",
